{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgtgx2NTWeCjQP8h9AkAB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The logit-lens result settles the sign. Neuron L22.573's output direction strongly promotes doubt tokens: \" wait\" is its top token out of 248k, and \"Wait\", \"Hmm\" and \"Actually\" all sit in the top few hundred. It barely touches \"So/Therefore/Final\" and \"</think>\" (rank about 4,500, small value). Its activation on texts A and B is almost always negative, with a long tail down to -8 and a maximum of only +0.27. In practice it therefore works as a context-gated doubt suppressor: when it fires strongly negative, it pushes \"Wait/Hmm/Actually\" down. Doubling its output strengthens that braking only where the network already decided to brake, which is a much more specific change than a global stop-thinking push. The earlier analysis also ran teacher-forced checks of an L16 edit (fwd_9) and this L22 edit (fwd_10), but the per-layer and per-neuron attribution behind the choice (NEU, NEU2, contrib, layer_mlp) is only in kernel memory. I will extract those numbers so the notebook records why n573 was chosen and whether other neurons (for example L22.998 or an L16 neuron) belong to the same braking circuit.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: earlier DLA over 98 doubt-decision positions (POS) ranked L22.n573 top; recover per-layer and per-neuron attribution numbers.\nprint('POS[:5]', POS[:5], 'P_', P_)\nprint('layer_mlp mean per layer', np.round(layer_mlp.mean(1), 3).tolist())\nprint('layer_mix mean per layer', np.round(layer_mix.mean(1), 3).tolist())\nfor nm, dd in [('NEU', NEU), ('NEU2', NEU2)]:\n    k0 = list(dd.keys())[:3]; v = dd[k0[0]]\n    print(nm, 'keys', k0, 'val type', type(v).__name__, (v.shape if hasattr(v, 'shape') else (len(v) if hasattr(v, '__len__') else v)))\n    for L_ in [16, 21, 22, 23]:\n        if L_ in dd:\n            vv = dd[L_]; s = str(vv[:6] if hasattr(vv, '__getitem__') else vv); print('  ', L_, s[:300])\ncm = contrib.mean(0); o = np.argsort(cm)\nprint('contrib mean: most neg', [(int(i), round(float(cm[i]), 3)) for i in o[:6]], 'most pos', [(int(i), round(float(cm[i]), 3)) for i in o[-6:]])\nprint('emb', np.round([emb.mean(), emb2.mean()], 3), 'inl', np.round(inl.mean(), 3), 'acts[:,573] mean', round(float(acts[:, 573].mean()), 3), 'acts23 shape', acts23.shape)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3490,"cache_read_input_tokens":16151,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3490},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4bcd242-3053-49df-a015-76e7a59477b0","uuid":"00abd8eb-a5fa-4132-a063-df502a1f546d","timestamp":"2026-11-10T05:24:52.837Z","request_id":"req_011Cgtgx2Dn4ntfEvi6HWQ9L"}
